  <prompt>
    Author the ACS messaging-channel ADR — **ADR-046** — superseding the reserved placeholder (FR-17, design §10). It codifies the messaging channel as an ADDITIVE extension of ADR-045, not a new pipeline. The placeholder already exists at `.claude/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md` (RESERVED, 2026-07-16) and `docs/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md` — this task turns them into full Accepted ADRs and flips the `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` row from Placeholder → Accepted.

    Codify, at minimum (design §10 + §14.7 lock the content):

    1. **ACS-as-transport / Dataverse-as-record.** Each chat message is a JSON transport artifact the BFF processes into a `sprk_communication` (type=`Message`=100000004) record + a transcript archive in SPE (via `ICommunicationArchiver`) — analogous to email's `.eml`. Dataverse is the system of record; ACS threads are reconstructible projections.
    2. **Uniform server-side token minting.** The BFF (trusted service) mints ACS `chat`-scoped tokens server-side for ALL participants (Entra→ACS exchange is VoIP-only, so even internal users get server-minted tokens); `communicationUserId` ↔ Dataverse identity mapping; NO ACS admin capability or token on any client in R1 (no client-side ACS SDK).
    3. **Inbound ingestor seam (net-new).** Add `ICommunicationChannelIngestor` alongside the shipped `ICommunicationChannelSender`/`ICommunicationArchiver` — completes ADR-045's stated-but-unbuilt intent; inbound = Event Grid → webhook → Service Bus job → normalizer → ingestor → persist → enrichment; idempotent dedupe on the ACS message id (also covers the outbound echo).
    4. **Membership as a projection.** ACS thread membership is a RECONCILED PROJECTION of Dataverse-derived access — never a second ACL. Open threads via `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034); private threads via the existing per-record sharing grant (mechanism from task 002).
    5. **First-class thread model.** `sprk_communicationthread` + `sprk_thread` lookup + thread↔channel child table + a direction-symmetric `IThreadResolver` grouping email reply-chains AND chat; point-forward.
    6. **Retention-minimized, per-customer ACS resource.** 30-day auto-delete (or delete-post-persist); ACS data location immutable at create → per-boundary resource via the provisioning orchestrator (ADR-027).

    Write BOTH forms: concise at `.claude/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md` (~120–160 lines, MUST/MUST NOT) and full history at `docs/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md` (rationale + alternatives + consequences). Update `.claude/adr/INDEX.md` (Placeholder → Accepted) and `docs/adr/INDEX.md`; ensure reachable from root `CLAUDE.md` §17; add the required `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry. Mirror exactly how ADR-045 was authored (email-r4 task 005). This is MAIN-SESSION ONLY (§3 write boundary).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke platform architect. Authoritative on the Communication architecture (ADR-045) and its channel-seam extensibility. Fluent in the project's concise ADR conventions (`.claude/adr/`, MUST/MUST NOT, ~120–160 lines) and the full-history form (`docs/adr/`). You author a binding ADR that every ACS/ingestor/thread/privacy task will cite.
  </role>

  <goal>
    ADR-046 exists in both concise (`.claude/adr/`) and full (`docs/adr/`) forms, codifying the six-part messaging-channel decision with MUST/MUST NOT rules; both ADR INDEXes show it Accepted (concise row flipped from Placeholder); reachable from root `CLAUDE.md` §17; `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has the entry; passes `/adr-check` against `spec.md` with no contradiction against existing ADRs. Tasks 020 (channel seams) + 021 (ingestor seam) build against a landed governance anchor.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Design §10 mandates a fresh ADR because ACS is a first-of-kind Azure resource for Spaarke (external transport, BYOI identity plane, per-customer provisioning, Event Grid ingress, a net-new ingestor seam). Landing it first — alongside the schema pass — enforces the discipline that the rest of the project references an authoritative anchor, exactly as ADR-045 anchored email-r4. Downstream `adr-check` + `code-review` on every ACS wave will cite ADR-046.

      §11 Component Justification (a NEW ADR + a NEW seam it codifies): (1) **Existing overlap** — ADR-045 covers channel seams but does NOT cover ACS transport, server token minting, the inbound ingestor seam, the thread model, or membership-as-projection; the placeholder was reserved precisely because these are net-new decisions. (2) **Extension instead** — the ingestor seam EXTENDS ADR-045's sender/archiver seam family (completing its stated intent), rather than a parallel contract; the ADR documents that. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without ADR-046, the ACS/ingestor/thread work has no binding anchor, so `adr-check` has nothing to validate the ACS decisions against and future channels/ISVs could re-litigate ACS-as-transport, client-token exposure, or a second ACL — the named failure modes design §10 guards.

      The ADR must correctly cite its neighbors: ADR-045 (the spine it extends), ADR-034 (open membership), ADR-028 (server token minting; no `new` credential), ADR-004/036 (job contract / background infra for capture + reconcile), ADR-007 (SpeFileStore transcript/attachment archive), ADR-024 (regarding-family thread anchor — no second mechanism), ADR-027 (per-customer resource provisioning), ADR-018/032 (kill-switch / Null-Object for feature-gated services + unconditional endpoints), ADR-015 (AI flags privilege, never decides), ADR-013 (AI facade if enrichment touched), ADR-038 (testing). Sibling ADR-047 is reserved for `notification-spine-r1` — do NOT claim it.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md (EXISTING placeholder → author full concise form)</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-046-acs-messaging-channel.md (EXISTING placeholder → author full form)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/INDEX.md (flip the ADR-046 row Placeholder → Accepted)</file>
      <file>docs/adr/INDEX.md (ADR-046 row)</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md (the spine this extends — cite + mirror structure)</file>
      <file>CLAUDE.md (§17 pointer reachability + CHANGELOG obligation)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">ADR number is **ADR-046** (reserved 2026-07-16). Sibling **ADR-047** is reserved for `notification-spine-r1` — MUST NOT claim it. Re-verify 046 is still the reserved messaging slot before writing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (§3 write boundary)">MAIN-SESSION ONLY. Sub-agents cannot write to `.claude/`. Execute from the main session, not a delegated Agent-tool sub-agent. An "Edit denied on `.claude/...`" from a sub-agent is the boundary working correctly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Author BOTH forms: concise (`.claude/adr/`, MUST/MUST NOT, ~120–160 lines) AND full (`docs/adr/`, rationale + alternatives + consequences). Mirror ADR-045's structure (Status / Context / Decision (MUST/MUST NOT) / Consequences / Related).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">ADR-046 is ADDITIVE to ADR-045 (extends the channel-seam family with an ingestor seam); MUST NOT introduce a second communication pipeline, second regarding mechanism, or second channel-provider contract.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchoring defers to the ADR-024 regarding family (extend, never replace).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Server-side ACS token minting only; central `TokenCredential`; MUST NOT `new` a credential/`ConfidentialClientApplication`. No client-side ACS SDK / no token to a browser in R1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Open-thread membership derives from `MembershipResolverService`; ACS membership is a reconciled projection — never a second ACL. Private grant = the task-002 mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project MUST NOT">Codify the owner-locked MUST NOTs: no Dataverse Activities / OOB email / portal comments; no native Teams chat capture; no client-side ACS SDK / composites in R1; AI never decides privilege (ADR-015).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every CLAUDE.md-touching PR MUST add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry.</constraint>
  </constraints>

